  "equipment_type": "Precision cooling unit (computer room air handler)",
  "applies_to": "Older Liebert precision cooling units on the Advanced Microprocessor (LAM) control, Challenger 3000, Deluxe System/3, Himod (LNA) and ICS, read over Modbus by a BASgatewayLX (Liebert Modbus table 27).",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for Liebert table 27 units: 73 objects (18 AI, 16 AO, 33 BI, 6 BO), all polled. Inputs give temperature, humidity, cooling, heating, humidify, dehumidify, economizer, stages, % capacity, unit status and the alarm bits; outputs set the setpoints, tolerances, alarm limits and delays, and switch the unit on/off and reheat/humidifier lockouts.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Liebert_Table_27_b_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Liebert Modbus table 27 (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/LiebertIntelliSlot.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 73 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Temperature Setpoint; Temperature Tolerance; Humidity Setpoint...); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance.",
    "Temperature/humidity setpoint and tolerance names appear twice (AO 52-55 and AO 66-69); the second set sits with the on/off and lockout controls."
  ],
